From 1d3f2e4f89c82d072a9133d9cce89c2f670815a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:56:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/19] Feed a pinned Helios verifier a signed OP head and
 untrusted state witnesses

op-head-relay serves Helios's consensus API from untrusted commitment sources:
pinned signer and chain, highest fresh block, nothing once stale, equivocation
stops serving, and blocks with transaction types the pinned verifier cannot
decode are refused. witness-gateway is the verifier's execution endpoint:
allowlisted methods, ordered failover, a create-only block-hash-pinned witness
cache used only when every upstream fails, and broadcast fan-out. Tests are
unit plus an offline end-to-end run against Anvil with synthetic test-key heads.

(cherry picked from commit 97785a40cda92c42d8b8e14ab9e9d25afc3332a2)
